  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.96,
      "text": "Welcome to Place Value and Estimation."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.8,
      "end": 4.84,
      "text": "Large numbers need not mean long calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.78,
      "end": 8.22,
      "text": "When you see a number close to a tidy round number,"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.22,
      "end": 11.88,
      "text": "you can take it apart, work with easier pieces, and put"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.88,
      "end": 12.98,
      "text": "it back together exactly."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.84,
      "end": 16.42,
      "text": "Let's see an easy, medium, and hard example."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.6,
      "end": 20.995,
      "text": "Easy problem. Work out three hundred and ninety-eight plus two"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.995,
      "end": 23.1,
      "text": "hundred and seven, without a calculator."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.08,
      "end": 27.05,
      "text": "First estimate: four hundred plus two hundred is about six"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.05,
      "end": 30.6,
      "text": "hundred. That tells us the size of a sensible answer before"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.6,
      "end": 31.36,
      "text": "we calculate."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.74,
      "end": 35.76,
      "text": "Write three hundred and ninety-eight as four hundred minus"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.76,
      "end": 39.58,
      "text": "two. Write two hundred and seven as two hundred plus seven."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.02,
      "end": 43.17,
      "text": "Together that is six hundred, plus five, giving six hundred"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.17,
      "end": 47.12,
      "text": "and five. Estimation checks the scale; careful adjustment"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.12,
      "end": 48.56,
      "text": "gives the exact result."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.91,
      "end": 53.13,
      "text": "Medium problem. Find fifty-seven times ninety-eight."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.67,
      "end": 56.99,
      "text": "Ninety-eight is close to one hundred, so imagine a rectangle"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.99,
      "end": 60.05,
      "text": "fifty-seven units high and one hundred units wide."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.69,
      "end": 62.95,
      "text": "Then remove a strip only two units wide."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.61,
      "end": 65.75,
      "text": "This picture is an equation waiting to happen."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.97,
      "end": 70.41,
      "text": "The large rectangle has area fifty-seven times one hundred,"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.07,
      "end": 73.01,
      "text": "which is five thousand seven hundred."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.47,
      "end": 77.25,
      "text": "The removed strip has area fifty-seven times two, which is one"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.25,
      "end": 77.91,
      "text": "hundred and fourteen."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.91,
      "end": 81.09,
      "text": "Subtracting gives five thousand, five hundred and eighty-six."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.81,
      "end": 86.39,
      "text": "That is close to our estimate, not a huge mysterious product."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.61,
      "end": 89.09,
      "text": "Here is the general habit."
    },
    {
      "start": 89.77,
      "end": 91.23,
      "text": "Look for a useful round number."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.91,
      "end": 94.99000000000001,
      "text": "Replace the awkward part by a tidy quantity plus or minus"
    },
    {
      "start": 94.99000000000001,
      "end": 95.89,
      "text": "a small adjustment."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.59,
      "end": 97.78999999999999,
      "text": "Keep that adjustment visible."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.35,
      "end": 101.15,
      "text": "The picture, the words and the equation should all describe"
    },
    {
      "start": 101.15,
      "end": 102.35,
      "text": "the same relationship."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.61,
      "end": 106.83500000000001,
      "text": "Hard problem. Which is greater: forty-nine thousand, nine"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.83500000000001,
      "end": 110.77000000000001,
      "text": "hundred and ninety-six times fifty thousand and four, or fifty"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.77000000000001,
      "end": 112.57,
      "text": "thousand squared minus seventeen?"
    },
    {
      "start": 113.45,
      "end": 115.53,
      "text": "Do not multiply out these enormous numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.19,
      "end": 119.35,
      "text": "Look at how far each factor is from fifty thousand."
    },
    {
      "start": 120.14,
      "end": 123.7,
      "text": "The factors are fifty thousand minus four and fifty thousand"
    },
    {
      "start": 123.7,
      "end": 127.7,
      "text": "plus four. The extra strips cancel, leaving fifty thousand"
    },
    {
      "start": 127.7,
      "end": 129.36,
      "text": "squared minus four squared."
    },
    {
      "start": 129.9,
      "end": 132.62,
      "text": "So the first expression is fifty thousand squared minus"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.62,
      "end": 136.66,
      "text": "sixteen. The second is fifty thousand squared minus seventeen."
    },
    {
      "start": 137.46,
      "end": 139.92000000000002,
      "text": "Therefore the product is greater by exactly one."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.46,
      "end": 143.1,
      "text": "A difference of squares replaces a mountain of arithmetic."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.76,
      "end": 149.12,
      "text": "Easy, medium, hard: compensation, an area model, and a hidden"
    },
    {
      "start": 149.12,
      "end": 153.38,
      "text": "identity. Each uses the same idea: break a number around a"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.38,
      "end": 156.04,
      "text": "convenient value, then account for the small change."
    },
    {
      "start": 156.78,
      "end": 157.62,
      "text": "Now it's your turn."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.92000000000002,
      "end": 160.9,
      "text": "Work through the next lesson problems and explain why each"
    },
    {
      "start": 160.9,
      "end": 161.88,
      "text": "adjustment is valid."
    }
  ]
}
